### Another Day, Another Recall

327 food recalls have already occurred this year; compare this to the all-time total of 685. What's even more alarming is that 90 of these recalls were Class I--the most severe, posing direct health risks. The breakdown is staggering: 184 allergen-related, 106 from salmonella contamination, and 80 involving foreign objects.

Some names keep resurfacing: Moonlight Packing Corporation, Albertsons Companies LLC, and Ambriola Co., Inc. are flagrant repeat offenders. Moonlight Packing even racks up an F grade with 11 recalls--each a Class I. The trend is clear: vigilance is the price of not being the next statistic.

### April 29th's Recall Wave

On the latest recall list, Costco's traditional madeleines stand out, caught sporting undeclared hazelnut and soy lecithin. Bombay Kitchen's Tikka Sev and Punjabi Mix are also under scrutiny for illegal coloring agents like FD&C Yellow #6. Meanwhile, Unistel Industries' ground allspice earns a Class I classification due to potential Salmonella contamination.

### A Repeat Performance?

With 67 brands marked as repeat offenders, it's clear some companies simply can't steer clear of trouble. Whether from negligence or systemic issues, the public pays the price--sometimes literally, with their health.
